  "warnings": [
    "THE BEAM SCHEDULE FOR THE WHOLE HOUSE. Eleven marks: B1, B1A, B2, B2A, B2X, B3, B4, B5, B6, B7, RB1, GB1, GB1X. Every beam mark used on the S-03 and S-04 framing plans is defined here.",
    "TWO MARKS ARE DRAWN AS FULL ELEVATIONS (B1,B1A and B2,B2A) and the rest only as cross-sections. The elevations carry bar-curtailment information the sections cannot: top bars run 1.25 m each side of the interior support and the extra bottom bars are cranked up 0.60 m from the support. Those figures are recorded under bar_cutoff_m on B1A and B2A.",
    "THE 'A' SUFFIX MEANS THE LONGER SPAN OF A CONTINUOUS PAIR, not a different section: B1 is the 4.00 m span and B1A the 5.00 m span of the same beam line, with the same 200x500 section and the same top steel but double the bottom steel (achieved with cranked bars, which is why section 1A-1A shows 4-Ø16 against the elevation's '2-Ø16 + 2-Ø16'). Same for B2 / B2A at 3 and 6 bars.",
    "B2X IS THE ONLY MARK WHOSE BARS ARE DECLARED AS RUN-THROUGH from another beam -- both its tags carry '(ต่อเนื่องจากคาน B2)'. It is the 1.20 m cantilever past grid 4 on S-03. The counts are recorded as printed, but a quantity take-off must not double-count them against B2.",
    "B5 IS THE OUTLIER: 3-Ø20 top and 5-Ø20 bottom with ป.Ø9 มม.@0.20 ม. Every other RC beam here uses Ø16 or Ø12 main bars with ป.Ø6 มม.@0.15 ม. B5 frames the stair well.",
    "DEPTHS IN USE: 700 (B7), 500 (B1/B1A/B2/B2A/B2X/B3/B5/GB1/GB1X), 400 (B4/B6/RB1). All beams are 200 mm wide without exception.",
    "GB1 and GB1X share one detail headed 'GB1, GB1X', so they are identical in section and reinforcement. What the X suffix distinguishes is not stated on this sheet.",
    "The elevation tags are written without a hyphen ('3Ø16 มม.') while the section tags use one ('3-Ø16 มม.'). Both are transcribed as printed in each place; they are the same bars.",
    "This sheet defines RC beams only. The steel beams BS1 (S-05) and the steel roof members are sized in their own sheets' หมายเหตุ blocks and appear nowhere here.",
    "NORMALIZED_2026-08-02: a packed size string (e.g. \"0.20x0.40\") was replaced by numeric width_mm/height_mm per schema 0.5; the printed text is kept in the matching *_printed_as field."
